hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20864","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Salil say: There was a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who would narrate to people until they crowded around him, so he would climb onto the roof of a house and narrate to people, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which verse in the Quran is greatest? He said: So a man said: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer. He said: So he placed his hand between my shoulders, and I felt its coolness between my breasts, or he said: So he placed his hand between my breasts, and I felt its coolness between my shoulders. He said: May knowledge please you, O Abu al-Mundhir, knowledge."
